e, then provides the GeModel excess-Gibbs derivative API. Examples See the UNIFAC implementation for a model using hyperdual AD. Inherits type~~gemodeladiff~~InheritsGraph type~gemodeladiff GeModelAdiff type~gemodel GeModel type~gemodeladiff->type~gemodel type~basemodel BaseModel type~gemodel->type~basemodel type~substances Substances type~basemodel->type~substances components Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Type Type This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a derived type to the parent type which it\nextends. Dashed arrows point from a derived type to the other\ntypes it contains as a components, with a label listing the name(s) of\nsaid component(s). Components Type Visibility Attributes Name Initial type( Substances ), public :: components Pure-component properties for the model’s component order. Type-Bound Procedures procedure( hyperdual_Ge ), public, deferred :: Ge function hyperdual_Ge(self, n, t) Prototype Evaluate the model’s primal excess-Gibbs energy in hyperdual form. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( GeModelAdiff ) :: self Concrete GE model; passed-object dummy. type( hyperdual ), intent(in) :: n (:) Component mole amounts as hyperdual values. type( hyperdual ), intent(in) :: t Temperature as a hyperdual value. Return Value type( hyperdual ) procedure, public :: excess_Cp public  subroutine excess_Cp (self, n, T, Cpe) Calculate Excess heat capacity. Read more… Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( GeModel ), intent(in) :: self Model real(kind=pr), intent(in) :: n (:) Moles vector real(kind=pr), intent(in) :: T Temperature [K] real(kind=pr), intent(out) :: Cpe Excess heat capacity [bar L / K] procedure, public :: excess_enthalpy public  subroutine excess_enthalpy (self, n, T, He, HeT, Hen) Calculate Excess enthalpy and its derivatives. Read more… Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( GeModel ), intent(in) :: self Model real(kind=pr), inte