icMixRule – yaeos ","text":"type, public, abstract :: CubicMixRule CubicMixRule Abstract contract for cubic-EOS mixture parameter calculations. Description Concrete mixing rules implement attractive, repulsive, and cubic\ndenominator parameter mixing, including derivatives needed for\nresidual properties and phase equilibrium. Examples See QMR , CMR , MHV , and HV_NRTL for implementations. Inherited by type~~cubicmixrule~~InheritedByGraph type~cubicmixrule CubicMixRule type~cmr CMR type~cmr->type~cubicmixrule type~cubiceos CubicEoS type~cubiceos->type~cubicmixrule mixrule type~hv HV type~hv->type~cubicmixrule type~hv_nrtl HV_NRTL type~hv_nrtl->type~cubicmixrule type~mhv MHV type~mhv->type~cubicmixrule type~qmr QMR type~qmr->type~cubicmixrule type~cmrtd CMRTD type~cmrtd->type~cmr type~gerg2008 Gerg2008 type~gerg2008->type~cubiceos srk type~qmrtd QMRTD type~qmrtd->type~qmr type~sddlc sDDLC type~sddlc->type~qmrtd Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Type Type This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a derived type to the parent type which it\nextends. Dashed arrows point from a derived type to the other\ntypes it contains as a components, with a label listing the name(s) of\nsaid component(s). Components Type Visibility Attributes Name Initial logical, public :: dn2 = .false. Calculate second-order mole-number derivatives logical, public :: is_D_ddlc = .false. Mixing rule D parameter depends on volume (density) Type-Bound Procedures procedure( abs_Bmix ), public, deferred :: Bmix subroutine abs_Bmix(self, n, bi, B, dBi, dBij) Prototype abs_Bmix Description Evaluate the repulsive mixture parameter and its composition derivatives. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( CubicMixRule ), intent(in) :: self Mixing-rule implementation. real(kind=pr), intent(in) :: n (:) Component mole amounts [mol]. real(kind=pr), intent(in) :: bi (:) Pure-component covolumes. real(kind=pr), intent(out) :: B Mixture covolume [L]. real(kind=pr), intent(out) :: dBi (:) Mole-number gradient of the mixture covolume. real(kind=pr), intent(out) :: dBij (:,:) Mole-number Hessian of the mixture covolume. procedure( abs_D1mix ), public, deferred :: D1mix subroutine abs_D1mix(self, n, d1i, D1, dD1i, dD1ij) Prototype abs_D1mix Description Evaluate the first denominator parameter and its composition derivatives. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( CubicMixRule ), intent(in) :: self Mixing-rule implementation. real(kind=pr), intent(in) :: n (:) Component mole amounts [mol]. real(kind=pr), intent(in) :: d1i (:) Pure-component values. real(kind=pr), intent(out) :: D1 Mixture parameter. real(kind=pr), intent(out) :: dD1i (:) Gradient of D1 with respect to mole amounts. real(kind=pr), intent(out) :: dD1ij (:,:) Hessian of D1 with respect to mole amounts. procedure( abs_Dmix ), public, deferred :: Dmix subroutine abs_Dmix(self, n, V, T, ai, daidt, daidt2, D, dDdV, dDdT, dDdV2, dDdT2, dDi, dDdTV, dDidV, dDidT, dDij) Prototype abs_Dmix Description Evaluate the attractive mixture parameter and its state/composition\nderivatives for a cubic mixing rule. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( CubicMixRule ), intent(in) :: self Mixing-rule implementation. real(kind=pr), intent(in) :: n (:) Component mole amounts [mol]. real(kind=pr), intent(in) :: V Total volume [L]. real(kind=pr), intent(in) :: T Temperature [K]. real(kind=pr), intent(in) :: ai (:) Pure-component attractive parameters. real(kind=pr), intent(in) :: daidt (:) Temperature derivatives of pure-component attractive parameters. real(kind=pr), intent(in) :: daidt2 (:) Second temperature derivatives of pure-component attractive parameters. real(kind=pr), intent(out) :: D Attractive mixture parameter. real(kind=pr), intent(out) :: dDdV Volume derivative of the attractive mixture parameter. real(kind=pr), intent(out) :: dDdT Temperature derivative of the attractive mixture parameter. real(kind=pr), intent(out) :: dDdV2 Second volume derivative of the attractive mixture parameter. real(kind=pr), intent(out) :: dDdT2 Second temperature derivative of the attractive mixture parameter. real(kind=pr), intent(out) :: dDi (:) Mole-number gradient of the attractive mixture parameter. real(kind=pr), intent(out) :: dDdTV Mixed temperature/volume derivative of the attractive mixture parameter. real(kind=pr), intent(out) :: dDidV (:) Volume derivative of the attractive mole-number gradient. real(kind=pr), intent(out) :: dDidT (:) Temperature derivative of the attractive mole-number gradient. real(kind=pr), intent(out) :: dDij (:,:) Mole-number Hessian of the attractive mixture parameter.","tags":"","url":"type/cubicmixrule.html"},{"title":"CriticalLine – yaeos ","text":"type, public :: CriticalLine CriticalLine Description This derived type is used to store a critical line between two fluids.\nThe critical line is calculated using the critical_line function. It\nuses the continuation method. Examples A critical line can be calculated between two fluids using the critical_line function.\nIn this example we calculate the critical of a binary mixture of\ncarbon dioxide and bicyclohexyl. use yaeos implicit none type ( CubicEoS ) :: model type ( CriticalLine ) :: cl real ( pr ) :: z0 ( 2 ), zi ( 2 ) real ( pr ) :: tc ( 2 ), pc ( 2 ), w ( 2 ) z0 = [ 1 , 0 ] ! Pure carbon dioxide zi = [ 0 , 1 ] ! Pure bicyclohexyl ! Setup the model tc = [ 30 4.21_pr , 72 7.0_pr ] pc = [ 7 3.83_pr , 2 5.6_pr ] w = [ 0.223621_pr , 0.427556_pr ] model = PengRobinson76 ( tc , pc , w ) ! Calculate the critical line cl = critical_line ( model , a0 = 0.99_pr , z0 = z0 , zi = zi , & ns0 = spec_CP % a , S0 = 0.99_pr , dS0 =- 0.01_pr ) Inherits type~~criticalline~~InheritsGraph type~criticalline CriticalLine type~equilibriumstate EquilibriumState type~criticalline->type~equilibriumstate CEP Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Type Type This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid 