, tol, max_iters) result(flash) flash_second_order Description Find a two-phase split at fixed temperature and pressure by minimizing\nthe reduced Gibbs energy with a second-order method. Arguments model : thermodynamic model ( ArModel or GeModel ). z : global mole fractions. T : temperature [K]. P_spec : pressure [bar]. k0 : optional initial K-factors. If omitted, Wilson factors are\n  used for ArModel and a stability analysis is used for GeModel . light_root : root used for the light phase with ArModel ( \"stable\" by default, \"liquid\" for a liquid-liquid split). iters : number of iterations used. tol : gradient-norm tolerance (default 1e-8 ). max_iters : maximum number of iterations (default 200 ). Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( BaseModel ), intent(in) :: model Thermodynamic model real(kind=pr), intent(in) :: z (:) Global mole fractions real(kind=pr), intent(in) :: T Temperature [K] real(kind=pr), intent(in) :: P_spec Pressure [bar] real(kind=pr), intent(in), optional :: k0 (:) Initial K-factors (y/x) character(len=*), intent(in), optional :: light_root Root of the light phase for ArModel ( \"stable\" or \"liquid\" ) integer, intent(out), optional :: iters Iterations used real(kind=pr), intent(in), optional :: tol Convergence tolerance integer, intent(in), optional :: max_iters Maximum iterations Return Value type( EquilibriumState ) Calls proc~~flash_second_order~~CallsGraph proc~flash_second_order flash_second_order proc~betato01 betato01 proc~flash_second_order->proc~betato01 proc~evaluate_gibbs evaluate_gibbs proc~flash_second_order->proc~evaluate_gibbs proc~k_wilson k_wilson proc~flash_second_order->proc~k_wilson proc~min_tpd min_tpd proc~flash_second_order->proc~min_tpd proc~solve_modified_cholesky solve_modified_cholesky proc~flash_second_order->proc~solve_modified_cholesky volume volume proc~flash_second_order->volume ln_activity_coefficient ln_activity_coefficient proc~evaluate_gibbs->ln_activity_coefficient lnphi_pt lnphi_pt pro