: lnKold real(kind=pr), private, dimension(size(z)) :: lnfug_x real(kind=pr), private, dimension(size(z)) :: lnfug_y character(len=2), private :: spec Flash specification [PT | VT] real(kind=pr), private, dimension(size(z)) :: x composition of liquid (molar fractions) real(kind=pr), private, dimension(size(z)) :: y composition of vapour (molar fractions)","tags":"","url":"proc/flash_no_beta_limits.html"},{"title":"continuation – yaeos","text":"public  function continuation(f, X0, ns0, S0, dS0, max_points, solver_tol, update_specification, postprocess, solver, stop) result(XS) continuation Trace a one-dimensional solution manifold of a nonlinear system. Description At each point the tangent is obtained from The tangent predicts the next point; solver (or the default Newton\ncorrector) then solves the residual equations there. The default\nspecification update selects the component of the tangent with the\nlargest magnitude, rescales the tangent to it and converts the step to\nthat variable (no step-size limit is applied). Tracing stops when the\ncorrector reaches its iteration limit (500), the residual is NaN, dS becomes zero, or stop returns true. The returned array has max_points rows; rows not reached\nbefore termination remain zero. Examples curve = continuation ( fun , X0 , ns0 , S0 , dS0 , & max_points = 100 , solver_tol = 1.0e-8_pr ) Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name procedure( continuation_function ) :: f Residual and derivative callback for . real(kind=pr), intent(in) :: X0 (:) Initial converged unknown vector. integer, intent(in) :: ns0 Index of the initially specified variable in X0 . real(kind=pr), intent(in) :: S0 Initial value of the specified variable. real(kind=pr), intent(in) :: dS0 Signed first step in the specification. integer, intent(in) :: max_points Maximum number of continuation points to store. real(kind=pr), intent(in) :: solver_tol Residual tolerance for the point corrector. procedure( process ), optional :: update_specification Optional callback to select the next specification and step. If absent,\nthe tangent component of largest magnitude is selected and the step is\nscaled using that component: ns = maxloc ( abs ( dXdS ), dim = 1 ) dS = dXdS ( ns ) * dS dXdS = dXdS / dXdS ( ns ) procedure( process ), optional :: postprocess Optional callback to modify the state or step after specification\nselection, for example to enforce bounds or change step direction. procedure( continuation_solver ), optional :: solver Optional point corrector. The built-in Newton solver is used by default. procedure( continuation_stopper ), optional :: stop Optional callback evaluated after each accepted point; true terminates\ncontinuation. Return Value real(kind=pr), (max_points,size(X0)) Stored solution vectors, one per row. Calls proc~~continuation~~CallsGraph proc~continuation continuation proc~full_newton full_newton proc~continuation->proc~full_newton proc~solve_system solve_system proc~continuation->proc~solve_system proc~full_newton->proc~solve_system none~dgesv dgesv proc~solve_system->none~dgesv Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Called by proc~~continuation~~CalledByGraph proc~continuation continuation proc~px_envelope_2ph px_envelope_2ph proc~px_envelope_2ph->proc~continuation proc~tx_envelope_2ph tx_envelope_2ph proc~tx_envelope_2ph->proc~continuation Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Variables Type Visibility Attributes Name Initial real(kind=pr), public :: S real(kind=pr), public :: X (size(X0)) real(kind=pr), public :: dF (size(X0),size(X0)) real(kind=pr), public :: dFdS (size(X0)) real(kind=pr), public :: dS real(kind=pr), public :: dXdS (size(X0)) real(kind=pr), public :: fval (size(X0)) integer, public :: i Loop/index variable. integer, public :: max_iters = 500 integer, public :: newton_its integer, public :: ns","tags":"","url":"proc/continuation.html"},{"title":"full_newton – yaeos","text":"public  subroutine full_newton(fun, iters, X, ns, S, dS, dXdS, point, max_iters, F, df, dfds, tol) Uses yaeos__math_linalg yaeos__auxiliar proc~~full_newton~~UsesGraph proc~full_newton full_newton module~yaeos__auxiliar yaeos__auxiliar proc~full_newton->module~yaeos__auxiliar module~yaeos__math_linalg yaeos__math_linalg proc~full_newton->module~yaeos__math_linalg module~yaeos__constants yaeos__constants module~yaeos__auxiliar->module~yaeos__constants module~yaeos__math_linalg->module~yaeos__constants iso_fortran_env iso_fortran_env module~yaeos__constants->iso_fortran_env Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Module Module Submodule Submodule Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a submodule to the (sub)module which it is\ndescended from. Dashed arrows point from a module or program unit to \nmodules which it uses. full_newton Description Correct one predicted continuation point with Newton’s method.\nThe correction solves at fixed specification value,\nhalving the Newton step until . It stops\nwhen or tol .\nIf iteration 10 is reached (for points after the first), is reset\nto the previous point plus 10% of the predictor step. On failure iters ends at max_iters + 1 . Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name procedure( continuation_function ) :: fun Residual/Jacobian callback. integer, intent(out) :: iters Newton iterations used for this point. real(kind=pr), intent(inout) :: X (:) Predicted vector; corrected solution on return. integer, intent(in) :: ns Index of the specified variable. real(kind=pr), intent(in) :: S Fixed specification value for this correction. real(kind=pr), intent(in) :: dS Step used to form the predictor. real(kind=pr), intent(in) :: dXdS (:) Tangent used by the predictor and recovery logic. integer, intent(in) :: point One-based continuation point number. integer, intent(in) :: max_iters Maximum Newton iterations for correction. real(kind=pr), intent(out) :: F (:) Residual at the corrected point. real(kind=pr), intent(out) :: df (:,:) Jacobian . real(kind=pr), intent(out) :: dfds (:) Derivative . real(kind=pr), intent(in) :: tol Residual (max-norm) convergence tolerance. Calls proc~~full_newton~~CallsGraph proc~full_newton full_newton proc~solve_system solve_system proc~full_newton->proc~solve_system none~dgesv dgesv proc~solve_system->none~dgesv Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Called by proc~~full_newton~~CalledByGraph p