m This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a submodule to the (sub)module which it is\ndescended from. Dashed arrows point from a module or program unit to \nmodules which it uses. Huron-Vidal NRTL mixing rule This is the Huron-Vidal mixing rule that includes the NRTL model\nmodified by Huron and Vidal. Description This is the Huron-Vidal mixing rule that includes the NRTL model\nmodified by Huron and Vidal. It is a mixing rule that allows to\nuse the NRTL model as an excess Gibbs energy model and can be\nsimplified to the classic quadratic mixing rules when the parameters\nare set to: Examples mixrule = HV_NRTL ( b , del1 , alpha , gji0 , gjiT , use_kij , kij ) Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=pr), intent(in) :: b (:) Pure-component covolumes [L/mol] real(kind=pr), intent(in) :: del1 (:) Pure-component values real(kind=pr), intent(in) :: alpha (:,:) NRTL non-randomness parameters real(kind=pr), intent(in) :: gji0 (:,:) Temperature-independent NRTL-HV energy parameters real(kind=pr), intent(in) :: gjiT (:,:) Temperature coefficients of the NRTL-HV energy parameters logical, intent(in) :: use_kij (:,:) Pairs where the quadratic-limit parameters with kij are used real(kind=pr), intent(in) :: kij (:,:) Binary attractive interaction parameters Return Value type( HV_NRTL ) Called by proc~~init_hvnrtl~~CalledByGraph proc~init_hvnrtl init_hvnrtl interface~hv_nrtl HV_NRTL interface~hv_nrtl->proc~init_hvnrtl Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an