mes and temperature. Description Undamped Newton correction of the saturation_F system, with unknowns . Pressure is an unknown\ntied to the incipient-phase pressure, and phase pressure equality is\none of the residuals. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( ArModel ), intent(in) :: model EOS used for phase properties. real(kind=pr), intent(in) :: z (:) Feed composition. real(kind=pr), intent(inout) :: X (:) Initial unknown vector; corrected state on return. integer, intent(in) :: ns Index of the specified variable. real(kind=pr), intent(in) :: S Specification value in solver coordinates. real(kind=pr), intent(in) :: tol Residual tolerance. integer, intent(in) :: max_iterations Maximum Newton iterations. integer, intent(out) :: its Iterations used. Calls proc~~solve_vxvyt~~CallsGraph proc~solve_vxvyt solve_VxVyT proc~saturation_f saturation_F proc~solve_vxvyt->proc~saturation_f proc~solve_system solve_system proc~solve_vxvyt->proc~solve_system proc~lnfug_vt ArModel%lnfug_vt proc~saturation_f->proc~lnfug_vt none~dgesv dgesv proc~solve_system->none~dgesv residual_helmholtz residual_helmholtz proc~lnfug_vt->residual_helmholtz Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Variables Type Visibility Attributes Name Initial real(kind=pr), public :: F (size(X)) Residual or scalar equation value. real(kind=pr), public :: Xold (size(X)) real(kind=pr), public :: dF (size(X),size(X)) real(kind=pr), public :: dFdS (size(X)) real(kind=pr), public :: dPdVy Pressure derivative with respect to the incipient-phase volume. real(kind=pr), public :: dPdVz Pressure derivative with respect to the feed-phase volume. real(kind=pr), public :: dx (size(X)) real(kind=pr), public :: dx_old (size(x)) integer, public :: nc Number of components.","tags":"","url":"proc/solve_vxvyt.html"},{"title":"pt_mp_flash – yaeos","text":"public  function pt_mp_flash(model, z, P, T) Uses yaeos__equilibria_stability proc~~pt_mp_flash~~UsesGraph proc~pt_mp_flash pt_mp_flash module~yaeos__equilibria_stability yaeos__equilibria_stability proc~pt_mp_flash->module~yaeos__equilibria_stability module~yaeos__constants yaeos__constants module~yaeos__equilibria_stability->module~yaeos__constants module~yaeos__models_ar yaeos__models_ar module~yaeos__equilibria_stability->module~yaeos__models_ar module~yaeos__models_base yaeos__models_base module~yaeos__equilibria_stability->module~yaeos__models_base module~yaeos__models_ge yaeos__models_ge module~yaeos__equilibria_stability->module~yaeos__models_ge iso_fortran_env iso_fortran_env module~yaeos__constants->iso_fortran_env module~yaeos__models_ar->module~yaeos__constants module~yaeos__models_ar->module~yaeos__models_base module~yaeos__substance yaeos__substance module~yaeos__models_base->module~yaeos__substance module~yaeos__models_ge->module~yaeos__constants module~yaeos__models_ge->module~yaeos__models_base module~yaeos__substance->module~yaeos__constants Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Module Module Submodule Submodule Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a submodule to the (sub)module which it is\ndescended from. Dashed arrows point from a module or program unit to \nmodules which it uses. pt_mp_flash Perform a multiphase flash at fixed feed composition, pressure, and temperature. Description This method will do stability analysis to detect the possibility of\nnew phases. For each new phase detected it will calculate a multiphase\nflash and repeat stability analysis until no new phases are detected. Examples result = pt_mp_flash ( model , z , P , T ) print * , result % np , result % x_l Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( ArModel ), intent(in) :: model Residual Helmholtz EOS. real(kind=pr), intent(in) :: z (:) Overall feed mole fractions. real(kind=pr), intent(in) :: P Pressure [bar]. real(kind=pr), intent(in) :: T Temperature [K]. Return Value type( MPEquilibriumState ) Calls proc~~pt_mp_flash~~CallsGraph proc~pt_mp_flash pt_mp_flash proc~min_tpd min_tpd proc~pt_mp_flash->proc~min_tpd proc~solve_mp_flash_point solve_mp_flash_point proc~pt_mp_flash->proc~solve_mp_flash_point ln_activity_coefficient ln_activity_coefficient proc~min_tpd->ln_activity_coefficient lnphi_pt lnphi_pt proc~min_tpd->lnphi_pt proc~tm tm proc~min_tpd->proc~tm proc~pt_f_np pt_F_NP proc~solve_mp_flash_point->proc~pt_f_np proc~solve_system solve_system proc~solve_mp_flash_point->proc~solve_system proc~lnphi_pt ArModel%lnphi_pt proc~pt_f_np->proc~lnphi_pt none~dgesv dgesv proc~solve_system->none~dgesv proc~tm->ln_activity_coefficient proc~tm->lnphi_pt proc~lnphi_vt ArModel%lnphi_vt proc~lnphi_pt->proc~lnphi_vt proc~volume~2 ArModel%volume proc~lnphi_pt->proc~volume~2 residual_helmholtz residual_helmholtz proc~lnphi_vt->residual_helmholtz get_v0 get_v0 proc~volume~2->get_v0 interface~newton newton proc~volume~2->interface~newton proc~newton_1d newton_1d interface~newton->proc~newton_1d Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interf