int from a submodule to the (sub)module which it is\ndescended from. Dashed arrows point from a module or program unit to \nmodules which it uses. critical_line Description Calculates the critical line between two mixtures using the\ncontinuation method. The two mixtures compositions are restricted to\nthe relation between them, by a parameter , which represents\nthe molar fraction of the second fluid with respect to the whole\nmixture.\nIteration count.\nAvoid compositions with negative values Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( ArModel ), intent(in) :: model Equation of state model real(kind=pr), intent(in) :: a0 Initial value real(kind=pr), intent(in) :: z0 (:) Molar fractions of the first fluid real(kind=pr), intent(in) :: zi (:) Molar fractions of the second fluid integer, intent(in) :: ns0 Position of the specification variable in (use spec_CP ) real(kind=pr), intent(in) :: S0 Specified value: itself for spec_CP%a , otherwise the logarithm of , or real(kind=pr), intent(in) :: dS0 Initial step size real(kind=pr), intent(in), optional :: v0 Initial volume [L/mol], defaults to the vapor root at , real(kind=pr), intent(in), optional :: t0 Initial temperature [K], defaults to real(kind=pr), intent(in), optional :: p0 Initial pressure [bar], defaults to integer, intent(in), optional :: max_points Maximum number of points, defaults to 1000 real(kind=pr), intent(in), optional :: maxP Maximum pressure [bar], defaults to 2500 type( EquilibriumState ), intent(in), optional :: first_point Optional initial point; overrides the initial guess with first_point%x(2) , Vx , T , P . logical, optional :: stability_analysis If .true. , check the stability of each traced critical state (default .false. ). Return Value type( CriticalLine ) Calls proc~~critical_line~~CallsGraph proc~critical_line critical_line df df proc~critical_line->df dfds dfds proc~critical_line->dfds dx dx proc~critical_line->dx dxds dxds proc~critical_line->dxds f f proc~critical_line->f proc