point from a submodule to the (sub)module which it is\ndescended from. Dashed arrows point from a module or program unit to \nmodules which it uses. saturation_pressure Saturation pressure calculation function. Description Calculates the saturation pressure of a multicomponent mixture with\na given molar composition n .\nIt is possible to calculate: Bubble point: kind=\"bubble\" Dew point: kind=\"dew\" Liquid-Liquid point: kind=\"liquid-liquid\" It will first try to converge a solution using a Newton method to\nsolve the equation updating at each step as the ratio of fugacities of the phases.\nIf the solution does not converge, it will use a full Newton method to\nsolve the system in with specified. On failure the returned state has kind = \"failed\" . Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( ArModel ), intent(in), target :: model EOS used to evaluate phase fugacities. real(kind=pr), intent(in) :: n (:) Composition vector [moles / molar fraction] real(kind=pr), intent(in) :: t Temperature [K] character(len=*), intent(in) :: kind [bubble|dew|liquid-liquid] real(kind=pr), intent(in), optional :: p0 Initial pressure [bar], defaults to the Wilson estimate real(kind=pr), intent(in), optional :: y0 (:) Initial guess used as to build ( y/z for bubble and liquid-liquid, z/y for dew); defaults to . integer, intent(in), optional :: max_iters Currently ignored: the full Newton solve uses the module variable max_iterations . Return Value type( EquilibriumState ) Calls proc~~saturation_pressure~~CallsGraph proc~saturation_pressure saturation_pressure interface~optval optval proc~saturation_pressure->interface~optval proc~k_wilson k_wilson proc~saturation_pressure->proc~k_wilson proc~lnphi_pt ArModel%lnphi_pt proc~saturation_pressure->proc~lnphi_pt proc~p_wilson P_wilson proc~saturation_pressure->proc~p_wilson proc~solve_tp solve_TP proc~saturation_pressure->proc~solve_tp proc~volume~2 ArModel%volume proc~saturation_pressure->proc~volume~2 proc~optval_character optva