d point: kind=\"liquid-liquid\" It will first try to converge a solution using a Newton method to\nsolve the equation updating at each step as the ratio of fugacities of the phases.\nIf the solution does not converge, it will use a full Newton method to\nsolve the system in with specified. On failure the returned state has kind = \"failed\" . Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( ArModel ), intent(in), target :: model EOS used to evaluate phase fugacities. real(kind=pr), intent(in) :: n (:) Composition vector [moles / molar fraction] real(kind=pr), intent(in) :: p Pressure [bar] character(len=*), intent(in) :: kind [bubble|dew|liquid-liquid] real(kind=pr), intent(in), optional :: t0 Initial temperature [K], defaults to 250 K real(kind=pr), intent(in), optional :: y0 (:) Initial guess used as to build ( y/z for bubble and liquid-liquid, z/y for dew); defaults to . integer, intent(in), optional :: max_iters Currently ignored: the full Newton solve uses the module variable max_iterations . Return Value type( EquilibriumState ) Calls proc~~saturation_temperature~~CallsGraph proc~saturation_temperature saturation_temperature interface~optval optval proc~saturation_temperature->interface~optval proc~k_wilson k_wilson proc~saturation_temperature->proc~k_wilson proc~lnphi_pt ArModel%lnphi_pt proc~saturation_temperature->proc~lnphi_pt proc~solve_tp solve_TP proc~saturation_temperature->proc~solve_tp proc~volume~2 ArModel%volume proc~saturation_temperature->proc~volume~2 proc~optval_character optval_character interface~optval->proc~optval_character proc~optval_integer optval_integer interface~optval->proc~optval_integer proc~optval_logical optval_logical interface~optval->proc~optval_logical proc~optval_real optval_real interface~optval->proc~optval_real proc~lnphi_pt->proc~volume~2 proc~lnphi_vt ArModel%lnphi_vt proc~lnphi_pt->proc~lnphi_vt none~wrap wrap proc~solve_tp->none~wrap proc~newton~2 newton proc~solve_tp->proc~newton~2 get_v0 get_v0 proc~volume~2->g