 (x, f, df) Pressure residual callback used by the GERG volume Newton solve. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=pr), intent(in) :: x Logarithm of the trial volume. real(kind=pr), intent(out) :: f Pressure residual [bar]. real(kind=pr), intent(out) :: df Pressure-residual derivative with respect to log-volume.","tags":"","url":"proc/volume~3.html"},{"title":"tm – yaeos","text":"public  function tm(model, z, w, P, T, d, dtpd) tm Evaluate Michelsen’s modified reduced tangent-plane distance. Description Alternative formulation of the reduced tangent plane function,\nwhere the test phase is defined in moles, which enables for unconstrained\nminimization. Examples Calculation of tm tpd_value = tm ( model , z , w , P , T ) Using precalculated feed data It is possible to calculate externally the feed d_i vector and use it for\nlater calculations. call model % lnphi_pt ( z , T = T , P = P , V = Vz , root_type = \"stable\" , lnPhi = lnphi_z ) d = log ( z ) + lnphi_z tpd_value = tm ( model , z , w , P , T , d = d ) References Thermodynamic Models: Fundamental and Computational Aspects, Michael L.\nMichelsen, Jørgen M. Mollerup. Tie-Line Publications, Denmark (2004) doi Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( BaseModel ), intent(in) :: model Thermodynamic model real(kind=pr), intent(in) :: z (:) Feed composition real(kind=pr), intent(in) :: w (:) Test-phase mole numbers vector real(kind=pr), intent(in) :: P Pressure [bar] real(kind=pr), intent(in) :: T Temperature [K] real(kind=pr), intent(in), optional :: d (:) vector real(kind=pr), intent(out), optional :: dtpd (:) Gradient of tm with respect to trial-phase mole amounts. Return Value real(kind=pr) Calls proc~~tm~~CallsGraph proc~tm tm ln_activity_coefficient ln_activity_coefficient proc~tm->ln_activity_coefficient lnphi_pt lnphi_pt proc~tm->lnphi_pt Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type B