ic :: work (size(A,1)*10) Numerical workspace. Interfaces interface subroutine dsyev(JOBZ, UPLO, N, A, lda, W, WORK, LWORK, INFO) LAPACK interface for a real symmetric eigenproblem. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name character(len=1) :: JOBZ Whether eigenvectors are computed. character(len=1) :: UPLO Triangle of the input matrix that is referenced. integer :: N Matrix order. double precision :: A (lda,*) Matrix/work array. integer :: lda Leading dimension of A . double precision :: W (*) Eigenvalues. double precision :: WORK (*) Workspace array. integer :: LWORK Workspace length. integer :: INFO LAPACK status code.","tags":"","url":"proc/eigen.html"},{"title":"find_hpl – yaeos","text":"public  function find_hpl(model, z, T0, P0, max_points) find_hpl Description Find a liquid-liquid phase boundary on the PT plane. At a specified\npressure.\nThe procedure consists in looking for the temperature at which the\nfugacity of a component in the mixture is higher than the fugacity\nof the same component in a pure phase. This is done for each component\nin the mixture. The component with the highest temperature is selected\nas it should be the first one appearing. If all components have a\nnegative difference then the mixture is probably stable at all\ntemperatures. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( ArModel ), intent(in) :: model Equation of state model real(kind=pr), intent(in) :: z (:) Mole fractions real(kind=pr), intent(in) :: T0 Initial temperature [K] real(kind=pr), intent(in) :: P0 Search pressure [bar] integer, intent(in) :: max_points Maximum number of points passed to the envelope continuation. Return Value type( PTEnvel2 ) Calls proc~~find_hpl~~CallsGraph proc~find_hpl find_hpl proc~lnphi_pt ArModel%lnphi_pt proc~find_hpl->proc~lnphi_pt proc~pt_envelope_2ph pt_envelope_2ph proc~find_hpl->proc~pt_envelope_2ph proc~lnphi_vt ArModel%lnphi_vt proc~lnphi_pt->proc~lnphi_vt proc~volume~2 ArModel%volume proc~lnphi_pt->proc~volume~2 interface