tract Interfaces abstract interface public  subroutine f_1d(x, f, df) Callback interface for a scalar residual and its derivative. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=pr), intent(in) :: x Current scalar iterate. real(kind=pr), intent(out) :: f Residual value . real(kind=pr), intent(out) :: df Derivative . Derived Types type, public :: Point Represents the single point of a line segment. Read more… Components Type Visibility Attributes Name Initial integer, public :: i Index of the first line segment integer, public :: j Index of the second line segment real(kind=pr), public :: x X coordinate real(kind=pr), public :: y Y coordinate Functions public  function central_numdiff (f, x, eps) result(df) Approximate the Jacobian of a vector function by centered differences.\nColumn i is evaluated using a perturbation ; thus\nthis routine requires nonzero entries in x for finite differences. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name public  function f(x) Vector-valued function differentiated by central_numdiff . Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=pr), intent(in) :: x (:) Function input vector. Return Value real(kind=pr), (size(x)) Function output vector. real(kind=pr), intent(in) :: x (:) Evaluation point. real(kind=pr), intent(in) :: eps Relative finite-difference step multiplier. Return Value real(kind=pr), (size(x),size(x)) Approximate Jacobian matrix. public  function derivative_d2xk_dnidnj (n) result(d2xk_dnidnj) Calculate the mole fraction second derivatives respect to mole numbers Read more… Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=pr), intent(in) :: n (:) Component mole amounts. Return Value real(kind=pr), (size(n),size(n),size(n)) , indexed (k,i,j) . public  function derivative_dxk_dni (n) result(dxk_dni) Calculate the mole fraction first derivatives respect to mole numbers Read more… Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=pr), intent(in) :: n (:) Component mole amounts. Return Value real(kind=pr), (size(n),size(n)) , indexed (k,i) . public  function dx_to_dn (x, dx) result(dn) Convert the mole fraction derivatives of a quantity (calculated\nso they do not sum to 1) to mole number derivatives (where the mole\nfractions do sum to one). Requires the derivatives and the mole fractions\nof the mixture.\nFrom Chemicals (Python) Read more… Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=pr), intent(in) :: x (:) Mole-fraction vector. real(kind=pr), intent(in) :: dx (:) Derivative of the property with respect to mole fractions. Return Value real(kind=pr), (size(x)) public elemental function interpol (x1, x2, y1, y2, x_obj) result(y) Linear interpolation. Read more… Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=pr), intent(in) :: x1 First point x value real(kind=pr), intent(in) :: x2 Second point x value real(kind=pr), intent(in) :: y1 First point y value real(kind=pr), intent(in) :: y2 Second point y value real(kind=pr), intent(in) :: x_obj Desired x value to interpolate Return Value real(kind=pr) y value at x_obj public  function intersect_one_line (lx, ly) result(intersections) Find the intersections of a single line with itself. Read more… Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=pr), intent(in) :: lx (:) X coordinates of the polyline vertices. real(kind=pr), intent(in) :: ly (:) Y coordinates of the polyline vertices. Return Value type( Point ), allocatable, (:) Detected non-adjacent segment intersections. public elemental function sq_error (exp, pred) Returns the squared relative error . exp must be nonzero; the result is dimensionless and elementally\napplicable to scalar or array values. Read more… Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=pr), intent(in) :: exp Reference or expected value; must be nonzero. real(kind=pr), intent(in) :: pred Predicted value being compared with exp . Return Value real(kind=pr) Subroutines public  subroutine intersects (x1, x2, x3, x4, y1, y2, y3, y4, s, t) Calculate 