 iteration.\nEach step is halved until its magnitude is at most half the current\niterate’s magnitude. This is a step-size safeguard, not a residual\nline search. Read more… Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name procedure( f_1d ) :: f Function and derivative callback. real(kind=pr), intent(inout) :: x Initial guess, replaced by the root estimate. real(kind=pr), intent(in) :: tol Absolute tolerance for residual and step size. integer, intent(in) :: max_iters Maximum Newton iterations. logical, intent(out) :: failed True when the iteration limit is exhausted. public  subroutine powel_hybrid (fun, tol, X, F, info) Solve a square nonlinear system with MINPACK’s Powell hybrid method. Read more… Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name public  subroutine fun(n, x, fvec, iflag) fun Description MINPACK residual callback for a square nonlinear system. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name integer, intent(in) :: n Number of unknowns and residuals. real(kind=pr), intent(in) :: x (n) Current unknown vector. real(kind=pr), intent(out) :: fvec (n) Residual vector. integer, intent(inout) :: iflag MINPACK callback control/status flag. real(kind=pr), intent(in) :: tol Convergence tolerance passed to MINPACK. real(kind=pr), intent(inout) :: X (:) Variables vector real(kind=pr), intent(out) :: F (:) Function values at solved point integer, intent(out) :: info MINPACK termination code.","tags":"","url":"module/yaeos__math.html"},{"title":"yaeos__equilibria_boundaries_phase_envelopes_px – yaeos","text":"Pressure-composition phase envelopes Continue a two-phase boundary at fixed temperature between limiting feeds. Description The continuation parameter interpolates the overall feed\nbetween two limiting compositions. The module returns pressure, phase\ncompositions, phase volumes, and detected critical points in PXEnvel2 . Examples line = px_envelope_2ph ( model , z0 , alpha0 , z_injection , first_point ) Uses yaeos__constants yaeos__math_continuation yaeos__equil