constants module~ar_interface->module~yaeos__constants module~yaeos__constants->iso_fortran_env Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Module Module Submodule Submodule Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a submodule to the (sub)module which it is\ndescended from. Dashed arrows point from a module or program unit to \nmodules which it uses. Used by module~~ar_interface~~UsedByGraph module~ar_interface ar_interface module~legacy_ar_models legacy_ar_models module~legacy_ar_models->module~ar_interface module~legacy_thermo_properties legacy_thermo_properties module~legacy_thermo_properties->module~legacy_ar_models Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Module Module Submodule Submodule Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a submodule to the (sub)module which it is\ndescended from. Dashed arrows point from a module or program unit to \nmodules which it uses. Variables Type Visibility Attributes Name Initial procedure( Ares ), public, pointer :: ar_fun Legacy residual Helmholtz callback pointer. procedure( initial_volume ), public, pointer :: vinit Legacy initial-volume callback pointer. Abstract Interfaces abstract interface public  subroutine Ares(z, v, t, Ar, ArV, ArTV, ArV2, Arn, ArVn, ArTn, Arn2) Ares Callback interface for legacy residual Helmholtz models. Description Calculates the residual Helmholtz energy and derivative outputs\nconsumed by the legacy property routines. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=pr), intent(in) :: z (:) Component mole amounts. real(kind=pr), intent(in) :: v Total volume [L]. real(kind=pr), intent(in) :: t Temperature [K]. real(kind=pr), intent(out) :: Ar Residual Helmholtz energy. real(kind=pr), intent(out) :: ArV Volume derivative of residual Helmholtz energy. real(kind=pr), intent(out) :: ArTV Mixed temperature/volume derivative of residual Helmholtz energy. real(kind=pr), intent(out) :: ArV2 Second volume derivative of residual Helmholtz energy. real(kind=pr), intent(out), dimension(size(z)) :: Arn Mole-number gradient of residual Helmholtz energy. real(kind=pr), intent(out), dimension(size(z)) :: ArVn Mixed volume/mole-number derivative of residual Helmholtz energy. real(kind=pr), intent(out), dimension(size(z)) :: ArTn Mixed temperature/mole-number derivative of residual Helmholtz energy. real(kind=pr), intent(out) :: Arn2 (size(z),size(z)) Composition Hessian. abstract interface public  function initial_volume(z, p, t) initial_volume Return an initial volume estimate for a legacy pressure solve. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=pr) :: z (:) Component mole amounts. real(kind=pr) :: p Pressure [bar]. real(kind=pr) :: t Temperature [K]. Return Value real(kind=pr) Initial total volume [L].","tags":"","url":"module/ar_interface.html"},{"title":"yaeos__adiff_hyperdual_ge_api – yaeos","text":"Hyperdual excess-Gibbs models Base type and derivative adapter for GE models using hyperdual AD. Description Extend GeModelAdiff and implement the hyperdual excess-Gibbs function.\nThe adapter extracts composition, temperature, and mixed derivatives to\nprovide the standard GeModel activity-coefficient interface. Examples See the group-contribution and NRTL model implementations for examples. References Hyperdual arithmetic is provided by hyperdual_mod . Uses yaeos__constants hyperdual_mod yaeos__models_ge module~~yaeos__adiff_hyperdual_ge_api~~UsesGraph module~yaeos__adiff_hyperdual_ge_api yaeos__adiff_hyperdual_ge_api module~hyperdual_mod hyperdual_mod module~yaeos__adiff_hyperdual_ge_api->module~hyperdual_mod module~yaeos__constants yaeos__constants module~yaeos__adiff_hyperdual_ge_api->module~yaeos__constants module~yaeos__models_ge yaeos__models_ge module~yaeos__adiff_hyperdual_ge_api->module~yaeos__models_ge module~hyperdual_mod->module~yaeos__constants iso_fortran_env iso_fortran_env module~yaeos__constants->iso_fortran_env module~yaeos__models_ge->module~yaeos__constants module~yaeos__models_base yaeos__models_base module~yaeos__models_ge->module~yaeos__models_base module~yaeos__substance yaeos__substance module~yaeos__models_base->module~yaeos__substance module~yaeos__substance->module~yaeos__constants Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Module Module Submodule Submodule Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a submodule to the (sub)module which it is\ndescended from. Dashed arrows point from a module or program unit to \nmodules which it uses. Abstract Interfaces abstract interface public  function hyperdual_Ge(self, n, t) Evaluate the model’s primal excess-Gibbs energy in hyperdual form. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( GeModelAdiff ) :: self Concrete GE model; passed-object dummy. type( hyperdual ), intent(in) :: n (:) Component mole amounts as hyperdual values. type( hyperdual ), intent(in) :: t Temperature as a hyperdual value. Return Value type( hyperdual ) Derived Types type, public, abstract, extends( GeModel ) :: GeModelAdiff Base type for hyperdual excess-Gibbs models. Read more… Components Type Visibility Attributes Name Initial type( Substances ), public :: components Pure-component properties for the model’s component order. Type-Bound Procedures procedure( hyperdual_Ge ), public, deferred :: Ge procedure, public :: excess_Cp procedure, public :: excess_enthalpy procedure, public :: excess_entropy procedure, public :: excess_gibbs procedure, public :: ln_activity_coefficient Subroutines public  subroutine excess_gibbs (self, n, t, Ge, GeT, GeT2, Gen, GeTn, Gen2) Evaluate excess Gibbs energy and requested derivatives by AD. Read more… Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( GeModelAdiff ), intent(in) :: self Model providing the hyperdual Ge function. real(kind=pr), intent(in) :: n (:) Component mole amounts [mol]. real(kind=pr), intent(in) :: t Temperature [K]. real(kind=pr), intent(out), optional :: Ge Excess Gibbs energy. real(kind=pr), intent(out), optional :: GeT Temperature derivative of excess Gibbs energy. real(kind=pr), intent(out), optional :: GeT2 Second temperature derivative of excess Gibbs energy. real(kind=pr), intent(out), optional, dimension(size(n)) :: Gen Mole-number gradient of excess Gibbs energy. real(kind=pr), intent(out), optional, dimension(size(n)) :: GeTn Mixed temperature/mole-number derivative of excess Gibbs energy. real(kind=pr), intent(out), optional :: Gen2 (size(n),size(n)) Hessian with respect to component mole amounts.","tags":"","url":"module/yaeos__adiff_hyperdual_ge_api.html"},{"title":"nonlinear_solvers – yaeos","text":"Damped Newton solver Solve small nonlinear systems using Newton steps and Armijo backtracking. Description newton_solve accepts a callback returning residuals and a dense Jacobian,\nupdates the initial guess in place, and reports a convergence code. It is\nimported by solve_TP in this source file, although that routine\ncurrently calls newton from yaeos__math_nonlinearsolvers instead. Examples call newton_solve ( fun , x , tol , max_iter , its , info ) Uses yaeos__constants yaeos__math_linalg module~~nonlinear_solvers~~UsesGraph module~nonlinear_solvers nonlinear_solvers module~yaeos__constants yaeos__constants module~nonlinear_solvers->module~yaeos__constants module~yaeos__math_linalg yaeos__math_linalg module~nonlinear_solvers->module~yaeos__math_linalg iso_fortran_env iso_fortran_env module~yaeos__constants->iso_fortran_env module~yaeos__math_linalg->module~yaeos__constants Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Module Module Submodule Submodule Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a submodule to the (sub)module which it is\ndescended from. Dashed arrows point from a module or program unit to \nmodules which it uses. Used by module~~nonlinear_solvers~~UsedByGraph module~nonlinear_solvers nonlinear_solvers proc~solve_tp solve_TP proc~solve_tp->module~nonlinear_solvers Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Module Module Submodule Submodule Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a submodule to the (sub)module which it is\ndescended from. Dashed arrows point from a module or program unit to \nmodules which it uses. Subroutines public  subroutine newton_solve (fun, x, tol, max_iter, its, info) Solve a nonlinear system by damped Newton iteration. Read more… Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name public  subroutine fun(x, f, J) Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=dp), intent(in) :: x (:) Current unknown vector. real(kind=dp), intent(out) :: f (:) Residual vector. real(kind=dp), intent(out) :: J (:,:) Residual Jacobian. real(kind=dp), intent(inout) :: x (:) Initial guess; last iterate on return. real(kind=dp), intent(in) :: tol Absolute residual convergence tolerance. integer, intent(in) :: max_iter Maximum Newton iterations. integer, intent(out) :: its Iteration count at termination. integer, intent(out) :: info 0 = converged (max-norm of residuals below tol ), 1 = iteration limit reached","tags":"","url":"module/nonlinear_solvers.html"},{"title":"yaeos__m_s_sp – yaeos","text":"Saturation-point nonlinear systems Residual equations, Jacobians, and point solvers for bubble, dew, and liquid-liquid states. Description The routines in this module encode saturation unknowns in logarithmic\ncoordinates and enforce isofugacity, material-balance, and specification\nequations. They are implementation-level solvers used by the public saturation_pressure and saturation_temperature routines. Examples Application code should call the public saturation-point functions rather\nthan these solver helpers. Uses yaeos__constants yaeos__models_ar module~~yaeos__m_s_sp~~UsesGraph module~yaeos__m_s_sp yaeos__m_s_sp module~yaeos__constants yaeos__constants module~yaeos__m_s_sp->module~yaeos__constants module~yaeos__models_ar yaeos__models_ar module~yaeos__m_s_sp->module~yaeos__models_ar iso_fortran_env iso_fortran_env module~yaeos__constants->iso_fortran_env module~yaeos__models_ar->module~yaeos__constants module~yaeos__models_base yaeos__models_base module~yaeos__models_ar->module~yaeos__models_base module~yaeos__substance yaeos__substance module~yaeos__models_base->module~yaeos__substance module~yaeos__substance->module~yaeos__constants Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Module Module Submodule Submodule Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a submodule to the (sub)module which it is\ndescended from. Dashed arrows point from a module or program unit to \nmodules which it uses. Used by module~~yaeos__m_s_sp~~UsedByGraph module~yaeos__m_s_sp yaeos__m_s_sp proc~saturation_pressure saturation_pressure proc~saturation_pressure->module~yaeos__m_s_sp proc~saturation_temperature saturation_temperature proc~saturation_temperature->module~yaeos__m_s_sp Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Module Module Submodule Submodule Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a submodule to the (sub)module which it is\ndescended from. Dashed arrows point from a module or program unit to \nmodules which it uses. Subroutines public  subroutine saturation_F (model, z, X, ns, S, F, dF, dPdVz, dPdVy) Evaluate the saturation residual system in log-volume coordinates. Read more… Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( ArModel ), intent(in) :: model EOS used to evaluate phase fugacities. real(kind=pr) :: z (size(model)) Feed composition real(kind=pr), intent(in) :: X (:) Unknowns integer, intent(in) :: ns Index of the specified unknown. real(kind=pr), intent(in) :: S Value imposed on unknown ns . real(kind=pr), intent(out) :: F (:) Saturation residual vector. real(kind=pr), intent(out), optional :: dF (:,:) Residual Jacobian. real(kind=pr), intent(out) :: dPdVz Pressure derivative with respect to the feed-phase volume. real(kind=pr), intent(out) :: dPdVy Pressure derivative with respect to the incipient-phase volume. public  subroutine saturation_TP (model, kind, z, X, ns, S, F, dF, dFdS) Evaluate a saturation residual system at fixed pressure or temperature. Read more… Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( ArModel ), intent(in) :: model EOS used for phase properties. character(len=*), intent(in) :: kind \"bubble\" , \"dew\" , or \"liquid-liquid\" ; any other value uses stable roots. real(kind=pr), intent(in) :: z (size(model)) Feed composition. real(kind=pr), intent(in) :: X (:) Unknowns integer, intent(in) :: ns Index of the specified unknown. real(kind=pr), intent(in) :: S Value imposed on unknown ns . real(kind=pr), intent(out) :: F (:) Residual vector. real(kind=pr), intent(out) :: dF (:,:) Jacobian with respect to the unknown vector. real(kind=pr), intent(out) :: dFdS (:) Residual derivative with respect to the specification. public  subroutine solve_TP (model, kind, z, X, ns, S, tol, max_iterations, its) Correct a fixed-pressure or fixed-temperature saturation point. Read more… Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( ArModel ), intent(in) :: model EOS used for phase fugacities. character(len=*), intent(in) :: kind \"bubble\" , \"dew\" , or \"liquid-liquid\" ; any other value uses stable roots. real(kind=pr), intent(in) :: z (:) Feed composition. real(kind=pr), intent(inout) :: X (:) Initial packed unknowns; corrected state on return. integer, intent(in) :: ns Index of the specified variable. real(kind=pr), intent(in) :: S Specified value of X(ns) (log coordinates) real(kind=pr), intent(in) :: tol Residual tolerance. integer, intent(in) :: max_iterations Maximum corrector iterations. integer, intent(out) :: its Iterations used. public  subroutine solve_VxVyT (model, z, X, ns, S, tol, max_iterations, its) Solve saturation equations using log phase volumes and temperature. Read more… Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( ArModel ), intent(in) :: model EOS used for phase properties. real(kind=pr), intent(in) :: z (:) Feed composition. real(kind=pr), intent(inout) :: X (:) Initial unknown vector; corrected state on return. integer, intent(in) :: ns Index of the specified variable. real(kind=pr), intent(in) :: S Specification value in solver coordinates. real(kind=pr), intent(in) :: tol Residual tolerance. integer, intent(in) :: max_iterations Maximum Newton iterations. integer, intent(out) :: its Iterations used.","tags":"","url":"module/yaeos__m_s_sp.html"},{"title":"yaeos__equilibria_multiphase_flash – yaeos","text":"yaeos__equilibria_multiphase_flash Module for multiphase flash calculations. Description This module contains routines and functions to perform multiphase flash\ncalculations. Examples type ( MPEquilibriumState ) :: mpfr type ( ArModel ) :: model real ( pr ) :: z ( 3 ), P , T , Tc ( 3 ), Pc ( 3 ), w ( 3 ) Tc = [ 374 , 31 , - 83 ] + 273 Pc = [ 221 , 74 , 46 ] w = [ 0.344 , 0.293 , 0.011 ] z = [ 0.03_pr , 1 - 0.13_pr , 0.1_pr ] P = 4 5.6_pr T = 19 0._pr mpfr = pt_mp_flash ( model , z , P , T ) print * , \"Number of phases:\" , mpfr % np print * , \"Phase compositions:\" do i = 1 , mpfr % np print * , \"Phase\" , i , \"composition:\" , mpfr % x_l ( i , :) end do print * , \"Reference phase composition:\" , mpfr % w (:) References Uses yaeos__constants yaeos__models_ar yaeos__equilibria_equilibrium_state module~~yaeos__equilibria_multiphase_flash~~UsesGraph module~yaeos__equilibria_multiphase_flash yaeos__equilibria_multiphase_flash module~yaeos__constants yae