unction. Read more… Components Type Visibility Attributes Name Initial integer, public :: Kexp Number of exponential terms integer, public :: Kpol Number of polynomial terms real(kind=8), public, allocatable :: c (:) Density exponents of the exponential damping factor real(kind=8), public, allocatable :: d (:) Density exponents real(kind=8), public, allocatable :: n (:) Term coefficients (polynomial terms first, then exponential terms) real(kind=8), public, allocatable :: t (:) Temperature exponents Subroutines public  subroutine get_original_parameters (ids, pures, binaries, components) Load the original GERG2008 parameters for the selected components. Read more… Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name integer, intent(in) :: ids (:) GERG2008 component identifiers type( Gerg2008Pure ), intent(out) :: pures (:) Pure-fluid parameters type( Gerg2008Binary ), intent(out) :: binaries (:,:) Binary parameters type( Substances ), intent(out) :: components Component properties public  subroutine original_parameters () Parameter table of the original GERG 2008 model Read more… Arguments None","tags":"","url":"module/yaeos__models_ar_multifluid_parameters_gerg2008.html"},{"title":"yaeos__solvers_pressure_equality – yaeos","text":"Fixed-volume two-phase pressure equality Solve phase pressure equality for a two-phase state at fixed temperature and total volume. Description The routine treats the heavy-phase volume as the Newton unknown and\nobtains the light-phase volume from the overall volume balance. It returns\nthe average phase pressure once the two phase pressures agree. Examples call pressure_equality_V_beta_xy ( model , T , V , beta , x , y , Vx , Vy , P ) Uses yaeos__constants yaeos__models_ar module~~yaeos__solvers_pressure_equality~~UsesGraph module~yaeos__solvers_pressure_equality yaeos__solvers_pressure_equality module~yaeos__constants yaeos__constants module~yaeos__solvers_pressure_equality->module~yaeos__constants module~yaeos__models_ar yaeos__models_ar module~yaeos__solvers_pressure_equality->module~yaeos__models_ar iso_fortran_env iso_fortran_env module~yaeos__constants->iso_fortran_env module~yaeos__models_ar->module~yaeos__constants module~yaeos__models_base yaeos__models_base module~yaeos__models_ar->module~yaeos__models_base module~yaeos__substance yaeos__substance module~yaeos__models_base->module~yaeos__substance module~yaeos__substance->module~yaeos__constants Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Module Module Submodule Submodule Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a submodule to the (sub)module which it is\ndescended from. Dashed arrows point from a module or program unit to \nmodules which it uses. Used by module~~yaeos__solvers_pressure_equality~~UsedByGraph module~yaeos__solvers_pressure_equality yaeos__solvers_pressure_equality module~yaeos__equilibria_flash yaeos__equilibria_flash module~yaeos__equilibria_flash->module~yaeos__solvers_pressure_equality module~yaeos__equilibria yaeos__equilibria module~yaeos__equilibria->module~yaeos__equilibria_flash module~yaeos yaeos module~yaeos->module~yaeos__equilibria Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Module Module Submodule Submodule Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a submodule to the (sub)module which it is\ndescended from. Dashed arrows point from a module or program unit to \nmodules which it uses. Subroutines public  subroutine pressure_equality_V_beta_xy (model, T, V, beta, x, y, Vx, Vy, P) Solve pressure equality between two phases at a given temperature,\ntotal volume, vapor molar fractions and compositions. Read more… Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( ArModel ), intent(in) :: model EOS used to evaluate both phase pressures. real(kind=pr), intent(in) :: T Temperature [K] real(kind=pr), intent(in) :: V Overall molar volume of the two-phase system [L/mol] real(kind=pr), intent(in) :: beta Molar fraction of light-phase real(kind=pr), intent(in) :: x (:) Molar fractions of heavy-phase real(kind=pr), intent(in) :: y (:) Molar fractions of light-phase real(kind=pr), intent(inout) :: Vx Heavy-phase molar volume [L/mol] real(kind=pr), intent(inout) :: Vy Light-Phase molar volume [L/mol] real(kind=pr), intent(out) :: P Pressure [bar]","tags":"","url":"module/yaeos__solvers_pressure_equality.html"},{"title":"yaeos__adiff_hyperdual_ar_api – yaeos","text":"Hyperdual residual Helmholtz models Base type and derivative adapter for models defined with hyperdual numbers. Description Extend ArModelAdiff , implement its hyperdual Ar function and the\ninherited volume initializer, and the adapter extracts the first and\nsecond derivatives required by the standard ArModel interface.\nThis is the intended user entry point for operator-overloaded AD; the\nadapter routines are its implementation details. Examples All that is needed is a derived type extending ArModelAdiff , a\nhyperdual-valued Ar function, and the inherited volume initializer. module newmodel use yaeos__adiff_hyperdual_ar_api , only : ArModelAdiff use yaeos__constants , only : pr use hyperdual_mod , only : hyperdual implicit none type , extends ( ArModelAdiff ) :: YourNewModel real ( pr ) :: a = 1.0_pr contains procedure :: Ar => arfun procedure :: get_v0 => v0 end type contains type ( hyperdual ) function arfun ( self , n , v , t ) result ( arval ) class ( YourNewModel ) :: self type ( hyperdual ), intent ( in ) :: n (:), v , t arval = sum ( n ) * t + self % a * v end function arfun function v0 ( self , n , p , t ) result ( vol ) class ( YourNewModel ), intent ( in ) :: self real ( pr ), intent ( in ) :: n (:), p , t real ( pr ) :: vol vol = self % a * sum ( n ) end function v0 end module newmodel References See example/extra/adiff_pr76.f90 and the user guide’s automatic-\ndifferentiation page for a complete implementation. Uses yaeos__constants hyperdual_mod yaeos__models_ar module~~yaeos__adiff_hyperdual_ar_api~~UsesGraph module~yaeos__adiff_hyperdual_ar_api yaeos__adiff_hyperdual_ar_api module~hyperdual_mod hyperdual_mod module~yaeos__adiff_hyperdual_ar_api->module~hyperdual_mod module~yaeos__constants yaeos__constants module~yaeos__adiff_hyperdual_ar_api->module~yaeos__constants module~yaeos__models_ar yaeos__models_ar module~yaeos__adiff_hyperdual_ar_api->module~yaeos__models_ar module~hyperdual_mod->module~yaeos__constants iso_fortran_env iso_fortran_env module~yaeos__constants->iso_fortran_env module~yaeos__models_ar->module~yaeos__constants module~yaeos__models_base yaeos__models_base module~yaeos__models_ar->module~yaeos__models_base module~yaeos__substance yaeos__substance module~yaeos__models_base->module~yaeos__substance module~yaeos__substance->module~yaeos__constants Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Module Module Submodule Submodule Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a submodule to the (sub)module which it is\ndescended from. Dashed arrows point from a module or program unit to \nmodules which it uses. Used by module~~yaeos__adiff_hyperdual_ar_api~~UsedByGraph module~yaeos__adiff_hyperdual_ar_api yaeos__adiff_hyperdual_ar_api module~yaeos__autodiff yaeos__autodiff module~yaeos__autodiff->module~yaeos__adiff_hyperdual_ar_api module~yaeos__models_ar_gerg2008 yaeos__models_ar_gerg2008 module~yaeos__models_ar_gerg2008->module~yaeos__adiff_hyperdual_ar_api module~yaeos__models yaeos__models module~yaeos__models->module~yaeos__models_ar_gerg2008 module~yaeos__models_cubic_mixing_rules_huron_vidal yaeos__models_cubic_mixing_rules_huron_vidal module~yaeos__models->module~yaeos__models_cubic_mixing_rules_huron_vidal module~yaeos__models_ge_implementations yaeos__models_ge_implementations module~yaeos__models->module~yaeos__models_ge_implem