oave, RKPR, and Mathias-Copeman temperature !! corrections. Each type evaluates \\alpha(T_r) and its first two !! derivatives with respect to reduced temperature, as required by !! `CubicEoS`. !! !! # Examples !! ```fortran !! type(AlphaSoave) :: alpha !! alpha%k = k_values !! call model%set_alpha(alpha) !! ``` use yaeos__constants , only : pr use yaeos__substance , only : substances use yaeos__models_ar_genericcubic , only : CubicEoS , AlphaFunction implicit none type , extends ( AlphaFunction ) :: AlphaSoave !! # AlphaSoave !! Soave temperature correction for cubic EOS models. !! !! # Description !! Evaluates \\alpha(T_r)=[1+k(1-\\sqrt{T_r})]&#94;2 componentwise and !! supplies its reduced-temperature derivatives. !! !! # Examples !! ```fortran !! alpha%k = k_values !! call model%set_alpha(alpha) !! ``` real ( pr ), allocatable :: k (:) !! k parameter. contains procedure :: alpha !! Alpha function end type AlphaSoave type , extends ( AlphaFunction ) :: AlphaRKPR !! # AlphaRKPR !! RKPR alpha function for cubic EOS models. !! !! # Description !! Evaluates \\alpha(T_r)=[3/(2+T_r)]&#94;k and its first two !! reduced-temperature derivatives componentwise. !! !! # Examples !! ```fortran !! alpha%k = k_values !! call model%set_alpha(alpha) !! ``` real ( pr ), allocatable :: k (:) !! k parameter. contains procedure :: alpha => alpha_rkpr end type AlphaRKPR type , extends ( AlphaFunction ) :: AlphaMathiasCopeman !! # AlphaMathiasCopeman !! Mathias-Copeman alpha function with component-specific coefficients. !! !! # Description !! For T_r \\leq 1: !!  !! \\alpha = \\left[1 + c_1(1-\\sqrt{T_r}) + c_2(1-\\sqrt{T_r})&#94;2 !!          + c_3(1-\\sqrt{T_r})&#94;3\\right]&#94;2 !!  !! and for T_r > 1 the Soave form with c_1 only, !! \\alpha = [1 + c_1(1-\\sqrt{T_r})]&#94;2. !! Each coefficient array has one value per component. !! !! # Examples !! ```fortran !! alpha%c1 = c1 !! alpha%c2 = c2 !! alpha%c3 = c3 !! call model%set_alpha(alpha) !! ``` real ( pr ), allocatable :: c1 (:) !! First Mathias-Copeman coefficient by component. real ( pr ), allocatable :: c2 (:) !! Second Mathias-Copeman coefficient by component. real ( pr ), allocatable :: c3 (:) !! Third Mathias-Copeman coefficient by component. contains procedure :: alpha => alpha_mc end type AlphaMathiasCopeman contains subroutine alpha ( self , Tr , a , dadt , dadt2 ) !! Soave \\alpha function and it's derivatives. class ( AlphaSoave ), intent ( in ) :: self !! Soave alpha parameters by component. real ( pr ), intent ( in ) :: Tr (:) !! Reduced temperature real ( pr ), intent ( out ) :: a (:) !! \\alpha real ( pr ), intent ( out ) :: dadt (:) !! \\frac{d\\alpha}{dT_r} real ( pr ), intent ( out ) :: dadt2 (:) !! \\frac{d&#94;2\\alpha}{dT_r&#94;2} associate ( k => self % k ) a = ( 1 + k * ( 1 - sqrt ( Tr ))) ** 2 dadT = k * ( k * ( sqrt ( Tr ) - 1 ) - 1 ) / sqrt ( Tr ) dadT2 = ( 1.0_pr / 2.0_pr ) * k * ( k + 1 ) / Tr ** ( 1.5_pr ) end associate end subroutine alpha subroutine alpha_rkpr ( self , Tr , a , dadt , dadt2 ) class ( AlphaRKPR ), intent ( in ) :: self !! RKPR alpha exponent by component. real ( pr ), intent ( in ) :: Tr (:) !! Reduced temperature real ( pr ), intent ( out ) :: a (:) !! \\alpha real ( pr ), intent ( out ) :: dadt (:) !! \\frac{d\\alpha}{dT_r} real ( pr ), intent ( out ) :: dadt2 (:) !! \\frac{d&#94;2\\alpha}{dT_r&#94;2} associate ( k => self % k ) a = ( 3 / ( 2 + Tr )) ** k dadT = - k * a / ( 2 + Tr ) dadT2 = - ( k + 1 ) * dadT / ( 2 + Tr ) end associate end subroutine alpha_rkpr subroutine alpha_mc ( self , Tr , a , dadt , dadt2 ) !! # alpha_mc !! Evaluate the Mathias-Copeman alpha function and its reduced-temperature derivatives. !! !! # Description !! Applies the low-temperature polynomial branch for T_r\\leq1 and !! the high-temperature continuation for T_r>1. !! !! # Examples !! Configure `c1`, `c2`, and `c3` by component and call the type-bound !! `alpha` procedure. class ( AlphaMathiasCopeman ), intent ( in ) :: self !! Component-specific coefficients. real ( pr ), intent ( in ) :: Tr (:) !! Reduced temperatures. real ( pr ), intent ( out ) :: a (:) !! Alpha-function values. real ( pr ), intent ( out ) :: dadt (:) !! First reduced-temperature derivative of alpha. real ( pr ), intent ( out ) :: dadt2 (:) !! Second reduced-temperature derivative of alpha. real ( pr ) :: sqrt_Tr ( size ( Tr )) real ( pr ) :: u ( size ( Tr )) real ( pr ) :: dudt ( size ( Tr )) real ( pr ) :: dudt2 ( size ( Tr )) sqrt_Tr = 1 - sqrt ( Tr ) ! The associate statement allows to abreviate the expresions associate ( c1 => self % c1 , c2 => self % c2 , c3 => self % c3 ) where ( Tr > 1 ) a = ( 1 + c1 * ( 1 - sqrt ( Tr ))) ** 2 dadT = c1 * ( c1 * ( sqrt ( Tr ) - 1 ) - 1 ) / sqrt ( Tr ) dadT2 = ( 1.0_pr / 2.0_pr ) * c1 * ( c1 + 1 ) / Tr ** ( 1.5_pr ) elsewhere u = - c1 * ( sqrt ( Tr ) - 1 ) + c2 * ( sqrt ( Tr ) - 1 ) ** 2 - c3 * ( sqrt ( Tr ) - 1 ) ** 3 + 1 dudt = ( 1.0_pr / 2.0_pr ) * ( - c1 + 2 * c2 * ( sqrt ( Tr ) - 1 ) - 3 * c3 * ( sqrt ( Tr ) - 1 ) ** 2 ) / sqrt ( Tr ) dudt2 = ( 1.0_pr / 4.0_pr ) * ( - 3 * Tr * c3 + c1 + 2 * c2 + 3 * c3 ) / Tr ** ( 3.0_pr / 2.0_pr ) a = u ** 2 dadt = 2 * u * dudt dadt2 = 2 * ( dudt ** 2 + u * dudt2 ) end where end associate end subroutine alpha_mc end module yaeos__models_ar_cubic_alphas","tags":"","url":"sourcefile/alphas.f90.html"},{"title":"psrk.f90 – yaeos","text":"This file depends on sourcefile~~psrk.f90~~EfferentGraph sourcefile~psrk.f90 psrk.f90 sourcefile~constants.f90 constants.f90 sourcefile~psrk.f90->sourcefile~constants.f90 sourcefile~groups.f90 groups.f90 sourcefile~psrk.f90->sourcefile~groups.f90 sourcefile~psrk_parameters.f90 psrk_parameters.f90 sourcefile~psrk.f90->sourcefile~psrk_parameters.f90 sourcefile~temperature_dependence.f90 temperature_dependence.f90 sourcefile~psrk.f90->sourcefile~temperature_dependence.f90 sourcefile~unifac.f90 unifac.f90 sourcefile~psrk.f90->sourcefile~unifac.f90 sourcefile~unifac_parameters.f90 unifac_parameters.f90 sourcefile~psrk.f90->sourcefile~unifac_parame