on another if the latter must be compiled before the former\ncan be. Source Code module yaeos__models_ge_group_contribution_groups !! # Group definitions !! !! # Description !! The [[Groups]] type stores the UNIFAC subgroups of a molecule and their !! occurrence counts. It is used by all group-contribution models. !! A molecule is represented by matching subgroup-ID and count arrays. !! !! # Examples !! ```fortran !! molecule%groups_ids = [1, 14] !! molecule%number_of_groups = [1, 1] !! ``` use yaeos__constants , only : pr implicit none type :: Groups !! # Groups !! Derived type used to represent a molecule and its UNIFAC groups. !! !! # Description !! Derived type used to represent a molecule and its UNIFAC groups. Is !! necessary to specify the subgroups ids and the subgroups on each !! molecule as shown in the example. !! !! # Examples !! !! ```fortran !!  ! Define toluene molecule groups !!  use yaeos, only: Groups !! !!  type(Groups) :: toluene !! !!  ! Toluene [ACH, ACCH3] !!  toluene%groups_ids = [9, 11] ! Subgroups ids !!  toluene%number_of_groups = [5, 1] ! Subgroups occurrences !! ``` !! !! # References !! 1. [Dortmund Data Bank Software & Separation Technology](https://www.ddbst.com/published-parameters-unifac.html) integer , allocatable :: groups_ids (:) !! Indexes (ids) of each subgroup in the main group matrix integer , allocatable :: number_of_groups (:) !! Occurrences of each subgroup in the molecule real ( pr ) :: surface_area !! Molecule surface area q real ( pr ) :: volume !! Molecule volume r end type Groups end module yaeos__models_ge_group_contribution_groups","tags":"","url":"sourcefile/groups.f90.html"},{"title":"auxiliar_functions.f90 – yaeos","text":"This file depends on sourcefile~~auxiliar_functions.f90~~EfferentGraph sourcefile~auxiliar_functions.f90 auxiliar_functions.f90 sourcefile~constants.f90 constants.f90 sourcefile~auxiliar_functions.f90->sourcefile~constants.f90 Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Source File Source File This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a file to a file which it depends on. A file\nis dependent upon another if the latter must be compiled before the former\ncan be. Source Code module auxiliar_functions !! # Auxiliary numerical functions !! !! # Description !! Relative-error and array-comparison helpers used in tests and !! consistency checks. The relative-error normalization is by the first !! argument, so callers should avoid a zero reference value. !! !! # Examples !! ```fortran !! if (allclose(reference, calculated, 1.0e-8_pr)) print *, \"consistent\" !! ``` use yaeos__constants , only : pr contains elemental function rel_error ( x , y ) !! # rel_error !! Return the absolute relative error with `x` as reference. !! !! # Description !! Computes |x-y|/|x|. The reference `x` must be nonzero. real ( pr ), intent ( in ) :: x !! Nonzero reference value. real ( pr ), intent ( in ) :: y !! Value compared against the reference. real ( pr ) :: rel_error rel_error = abs ( x - y ) / abs ( x ) end function rel_error function allclose ( x , y , rtol ) !! Check whether all elements of two arrays agree within `rtol`. real ( pr ), intent ( in ) :: x (:) !! First array real ( pr ), intent ( in ) :: y (:) !! Second array real ( pr ), intent ( in ) :: rtol !! Relative tolerance logical :: allclose allclose = maxval ( rel_error ( x , y )) < rtol if (. not . allclose ) then print * , \"Max relative error:\" , maxval ( rel_error ( x , y )) print * , \"x:\" , x print * , \"y:\" , y end if end function allclose end module auxiliar_functions","tags":"","url":"sourcefile/auxiliar_functions.f90.html"},{"title":"generalized_isoline.f90 – yaeos","text":"This file depends on sourcefile~~generalized_isoline.f90~~EfferentGraph sourcefile~generalized_isoline.f90 generalized_isoline.f90 sourcefile~ar_models.f90 ar_models.f90 sourcefile~generalized_isoline.f90->sourcefile~ar_models.f90 sourcefile~constants.f90 constants.f90 sourcefile~gen