ntity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a file to a file which it depends on. A file\nis dependent upon another if the latter must be compiled before the former\ncan be. Source Code module yaeos !! # yaeos thermodynamic library !! Public top-level module for EOS properties and phase-equilibrium calculations. !! !! # Description !! This module re-exports the shared constants, component data, model types, !! consistency tools, and phase-equilibrium procedures. Most users can start !! with `use yaeos` and then construct a model, evaluate properties, and run !! equilibrium routines without importing implementation submodules. !! !! The main API groups are: !! !! - [[yaeos__constants(module)]]: Units, real precision, and shared constants. !! - [[yaeos__consistency(module)]]: Numerical consistency checks for models. !! - [[yaeos__substance(module)]]: Component names and pure-fluid properties. !! - [[yaeos__models(module)]]: EOS and excess-Gibbs models and base types. !! - [[yaeos__equilibria(module)]]: Stability, saturation, flash, and critical routines. !! !! # Examples !! ```fortran !! use yaeos !! class(ArModel), allocatable :: model !! type(EquilibriumState) :: result !! real(pr) :: n(2) !! real(pr) :: z(2) !! real(pr) :: Tc(2) !! real(pr) :: Pc(2) !! real(pr) :: omega(2) !! real(pr) :: V !! real(pr) :: T !! real(pr) :: P !! model = PengRobinson76(Tc, Pc, omega) !! call model%pressure(n, V, T, P) !! z = n / sum(n) !! result = flash(model, z, T, p_spec=P) !! ``` use yaeos__constants use yaeos__consistency use yaeos__substance use yaeos__models use yaeos__equilibria character ( len =* ), parameter :: version = \"4.5.5\" !! This version. end module yaeos","tags":"","url":"sourcefile/yaeos.f90.html"},{"title":"pure_critical_solver.f90 – yaeos","text":"This file depends on sourcefile~~pure_critical_solver.f90~~EfferentGraph sourcefile~pure_critical_solver.f90 pure_critical_solver.f90 sourcefile~ar_models.f90 ar_models.f90 sourcefile~pure_critical_solver.f90->sourcefile~ar_models.f90 sourcefile~constants.f90 constants.f90 sourcefile~pure_critical_solver.f90->sourcefile~constants.f90 sourcefile~pure_saturation.f90 pure_saturation.f90 sourcefile~pure_critical_solver.f90->sourcefile~pure_saturation.f90 sourcefile~ar_models.f90->sourcefile~constants.f90 sourcefile~base.f90 base.f90 sourcefile~ar_models.f90->sourcefile~base.f90 sourcefile~math.f90 math.f90 sourcefile~ar_models.f90->sourcefile~math.f90 sourcefile~pure_saturation.f90->sourcefile~ar_models.f90 sourcefile~pure_saturation.f90->sourcefile~constants.f90 sourcefile~auxiliar.f90~2 auxiliar.f90 sourcefile~pure_saturation.f90->sourcefile~auxiliar.f90~2 sourcefile~continuation.f90 continuation.f90 sourcefile~pure_saturation.f90->sourcefile~continuation.f90 sourcefile~linalg.f90 linalg.f90 sourcefile~pure_saturation.f90->sourcefile~linalg.f90 sourcefile~auxiliar.f90~2->sourcefile~constants.f90 sourcefile~substance.f90 substance.f90 sourcefile~base.f90->sourcefile~substance.f90 sourcefile~continuation.f90->sourcefile~constants.f90 sourcefile~continuation.f90->sourcefile~auxiliar.f90~2 sourcefile~continuation.f90->sourcefile~linalg.f90 sourcefile~linalg.f90->sourcefile~constants.f90 sourcefile~linalg.f90->sourcefile~auxiliar.f90~2 sourcefile~math.f90->sourcefile~constants.f90 sourcefile~math.f90->sourcefile~auxiliar.f90~2 sourcefile~math.f90->sourcefile~continuation.f90 sourcefile~math.f90->sourcefile~linalg.f90 sourcefile~substance.f90->sourcefile~constants.f90 Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Source File Source File This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a file to a file which it depends on. A file\nis dependent upon another if the latter must be compiled before the former\ncan be. Files dependent on this one sourcefile~~pure_critical_solver.f90~~AfferentGraph sourcefile~pure_critical_solver.f90 pure_critical_solver.f90 sourcefile~pc_saft.f90 pc_saft.f90 sourcefile~pc_saft.f90->sourcefile~pure_critical_solver.f90 sourcefile~models.f90 models.f90 sourcefile~models.f90->sourcefile~pc_saft.f90 sourcefile~fluids.f90 fluids.f90 sourcefile~fluids.f90->sourcefile~models.f90 sourcefile~yaeos.f90 yaeos.f90 sourcefile~yaeos.f90->sourcefile~models.f90 Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Source File Source File This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a file to a file which it depends on. A file\nis dependent upon another if the latter must be compiled before the former\ncan be. Source Code module yaeos__critical_pure_point_solver !! # Pure-component critical-point solver !! Find pure-fluid critical constants for each component in an EOS model. !! !! # Description !! The critical point of a pure component is defined by the conditions: !! !!  !! \\frac{\\partial P}{\\partial V} = 0, \\quad \\frac{\\partial&#94;2 P}{\\partial V&#94;2} = 0 !!  !! !! This module solves the resulting nonlinear system in the variables !! `(V, T)` using a Newton-Raphson iteration. Each residual is evaluated !! from the equation-of-state pressure and its numerical derivatives. !! !! # Examples !! ```fortran !! call find_critical_points_all_components(model, nc, Vc, Tc, Pc, converged) !! ``` use yaeos__constants , only : pr use yaeos__models_ar , only : ArModel implicit none private public :: find_critical_points_all_components integer , parameter :: MAX_ITER = 151 !! Maximum Newton iterations per component. real ( pr ), parameter :: TOL_RES = 2.0e-8_pr !! Convergence threshold for the critical residual norm. real ( pr ), parameter :: TOL_STEP = 2.0e-6_pr !! Convergence threshold for the Newton step norm. ! Steps for numerical derivatives real ( pr ), parameter :: DV_STEP = 2.0e-4_pr !! Finite-difference increment in volume [L/mol]. real ( pr ), parameter :: DT_STEP = 2.0e-2_pr !! Finite-difference increment in temperature [K]. contains ! ======================================================================== ! MAIN ROUTINE: Find critical point for each pure component ! ======================================================================== subroutine find_critical_points_all_components ( model , nc , Vc , Tc , Pc , converged ) !! # find_critical_points_all_components !! Estimate pure-component critical constants for every model component. !! !! # Description !! For each component, first obtains a starting estimate from pure-fluid !! saturation calculations, then solves the criticality equations !! P_V=0 and P_{VV}=0 with a two-variable Newton iteration. !! A failed solve is reported in `converged`; the corresponding output !! values contain the final iterate and must not be treated as validated !! critical constants. !! !! # Examples !! ```fortran !! call find_critical_points_all_components(model, nc, Vc, Tc, Pc, ok) !! ``` class ( ArModel ), intent ( in ) :: model !! Equation of state used for pure-fluid saturation properties. integer , intent ( in ) :: nc !! Number of components; must match the model. real ( pr ), intent ( out ) :: Vc ( nc ) !! Critical molar volumes [L/mol]. real ( pr ), intent ( out ) :: Tc ( nc ) !! Critical temperatures [K]. real ( pr ), intent ( out ) :: Pc ( nc ) !! Critical pressures [bar]. logical , intent ( out ) :: converged ( nc ) !! True for components whose solve converged. integer :: i !! Loop/index variable. real ( pr ) :: V_init real ( pr ) :: T_init logical :: conv ! Fixed: Loop should usually start at 1 to cover all components do i = 1 , nc call estimate_critical_point ( model , i , nc , V_init , T_init ) call solve_critical_point ( model , nc , i , V_init , T_init , Vc ( i ), Tc ( i ), Pc ( i ), conv ) converged ( i ) = conv end do end subroutine find_critical_points_all_components ! ======================================================================== ! INITIAL ESTIMATE of critical point ! ======================================================================== subroutine estimate_critical_point ( model , i , nc , V_est , T_est ) !! # estimate_critical_point !! Construct an initial pure-component critical-point estimate. !! !! # Description !! Uses successive pure-fluid saturation calculations and the ratio of !! vapor to liquid volume to move the trial temperature toward the !! critical region. The estimates are initial guesses, not final results. use yaeos__equilibria_boundaries_pure_saturation , only : pure_saturation_line , PurePsat class ( ArModel ), intent ( in ) :: model !! Equation of state used to evaluate pressure and derivatives. integer , intent ( in ) :: i !! One-based component index. integer , intent ( in ) :: nc !! Number of components in the model. real ( pr ), intent ( out ) :: V_est !! Estimated critical volume [L/mol]. real ( pr ), intent ( out ) :: T_est !! Estimated critical temperature [K]. real ( pr ) :: z ( nc ) !! Feed or overall composition. real ( pr ) :: T real ( pr ) :: P_sat real ( pr ) :: VL real ( pr ) :: VV real ( pr ) :: ratio real ( pr ) :: dT logical :: psat_converged integer :: iter !! Iteration count. type ( PurePsat ) :: psat !! Declared saturation-line result; currently unused by this estimate. z = 0.0_pr z ( i ) = 1.0_pr ! Initial temperature heuristic scan T = 15 0.0_pr V_est = 0.15_pr T_est = T iter = 0 do while (. true . . and . iter < 100 ) P_sat = model % Psat_pure ( i , T , Vl = VL , Vv = Vv , converged = psat_converged ) iter = iter + 1 if ( abs ( Vv - Vl ) > 1e-3 ) then ratio = Vv / VL if ( ratio < 10_pr ) then T_est = T V_est = Vl return end if ! Advance temperature upward towards Tc dT = 0.08_pr * log ( ratio ) dT = sign ( min ( abs ( dT ), 0.1_pr ), dT ) T = T * ( 1.0_pr + dT ) else ! Step temperature down if above pseudo-critical or single phase T = T * 0.75 end if end do end subroutine estimate_critical_point ! ======================================================================== ! SOLVER: Newton-Raphson 2D to solve [dPdV, d²PdV²] = 0 ! ======================================================================== subroutine solve_critical_point ( model , nc , i_comp , V_init , T_init , Vc , Tc , Pc , converged ) !! # solve_critical_point !! Solve the pure-component criticality equations from an initial guess. !! !! # Description !! The residual vector is (P_V,P_{VV}). Its Jacobian with respect to !! (V,T) is approximated by centered finite differences, and a direct !! 2-by-2 Newton step is applied. Non-positive trial volume or temperature !! is reset to half the corresponding initial value. class ( ArModel ), intent ( in ) :: model !! Equation of state used for pressure derivatives. integer , intent ( in ) :: nc !! Number of components. integer , intent ( in ) :: i_comp !! One-based index of the pure component. real ( pr ), intent ( in ) :: V_init !! Initial molar volume [L/mol]. real ( pr ), intent ( in ) :: T_init !! Initial temperature [K]. real ( pr ), intent ( out ) :: Vc !! Critical molar volume [L/mol]. real ( pr ), intent ( out ) :: Tc !! Critical temperature [K]. real ( pr ), intent ( out ) :: Pc !! Critical pressure [bar]. logical , intent ( out ) :: converged !! Whether either convergence test succeeded. real ( pr ) :: V real ( pr ) :: T real ( pr ) :: P real ( pr ) :: f1 real ( pr ) :: f2 real ( pr ) :: norm_f real ( pr ) :: J ( 2 , 2 ) !! Jacobian matrix. real ( pr ) :: J_inv ( 2 , 2 ) real ( pr ) :: det real ( pr ) :: dX ( 2 ) integer :: iter !! Iteration count. V = V_init T = T_init converged = . false . ! Newton-Raphson loop do iter = 1 , MAX_ITER ! Evaluate residuals: f1 = dP/dV,  f2 = d²P/dV² call residual_critical_eqs ( model , nc , i_comp , V , T , f1 , f2 , P ) norm_f = sqrt ( f1 ** 2 + f2 ** 2 ) if ( norm_f < TOL_RES ) then converged = . true . Vc = V ; Tc = T ; Pc = P return end if ! Calculate 2x2 Jacobian numerically call jacobian_critical_eqs ( model , nc , i_comp , V , T , J ) ! Invert 2x2 matrix det = J ( 1 , 1 ) * J ( 2 , 2 ) - J ( 1 , 2 ) * J ( 2 , 1 ) if ( abs ( det ) < 2.0e-12_pr ) then Vc = V ; Tc = T ; Pc = P return ! Singular Jacobian end if J_inv ( 1 , 1 ) = J ( 2 , 2 ) / det J_inv ( 1 , 2 ) = - J ( 1 , 2 ) / det J_inv ( 2 , 1 ) = - J ( 2 , 1 ) / det J_inv ( 2 , 2 ) = J ( 1 , 1 ) / det ! Newton step: dX = -J_inv * f dX ( 1 ) = - ( J_inv ( 1 , 1 ) * f1 + J_inv ( 1 , 2 ) * f2 ) dX ( 2 ) = - ( J_inv ( 2 , 1 ) * f1 + J_inv ( 2 , 2 ) * f2 ) ! Update variables V = V + dX ( 1 ) T = T + dX ( 2 ) ! Safeguards if ( V <= 0.0_pr ) V = V_init / 2.0_pr if ( T <= 0.0_pr ) T = T_init / 2.0_pr ! Step convergence criterion if ( sqrt ( dX ( 1 ) ** 2 + dX ( 2 ) ** 2 ) < TOL_STEP . and . norm_f < 1 0.0_pr * TOL_RES ) then converged = . true . Vc = V ; Tc = T ; Pc = P return end if end do Vc = V ; Tc = T ; Pc = P converged = . false . end subroutine solve_critical_point ! ======================================================================== ! Evaluate residuals: [f1, f2] = [dP/dV, d²P/dV²] ! ======================================================================== subroutine residual_critical_eqs ( model , nc , i_comp , V , T , f1 , f2 , P ) !! # residual_critical_eqs !! Evaluate the two criticality residuals at a pure-fluid state. !! !! # Description !! Computes f_1=P_V from the EOS and f_2=P_{VV} by a centered !! finite difference of P_V in volume. class ( ArModel ), intent ( in ) :: model !! Equation of state used for pressure derivatives. integer , intent ( in ) :: i_comp !! One-based index of the pure component. integer , intent ( in ) :: nc !! Number of components. real ( pr ), intent ( in ) :: V !! Total volume [L]. real ( pr ), intent ( in ) :: T !! Temperature [K]. real ( pr ), intent ( out ) :: f1 !! First criticality residual, pressure differentiated with respect to volume. real ( pr ), intent ( out ) :: f2 !! Second criticality residual, pressure differentiated twice with respect to volume. real ( pr ), intent ( out ) :: P !! Pressure [bar]. real ( pr ) :: z ( nc ) real ( pr ) :: dPdV real ( pr ) :: dPdV_plus real ( pr ) :: dPdV_minus real ( pr ) :: Pin ! Fixed: Pure component mole fraction is 1.0, others 0.0 z = 0.0_pr z ( i_comp ) = 1.0_pr call model % pressure ( z , V , T , P , dPdV = dPdV ) f1 = dPdV call model % pressure ( z , V + DV_STEP , T , Pin , dPdV = dPdV_plus ) call model % pressure ( z , V - DV_STEP , T , Pin , dPdV = dPdV_minus ) f2 = ( dPdV_plus - dPdV_minus ) / ( 2.0_pr * DV_STEP ) end subroutine residual_critical_eqs ! ======================================================================== ! Jacobian: matrix of derivatives ∂f_i / ∂x_j ! ======================================================================== subroutine jacobian_critical_eqs ( model , nc , i_comp , V , T , J ) !! # jacobian_critical_eqs !! Approximate the Jacobian of (P_V,P_{VV}) with respect to (V,T). !! !! # Description !! Centered finite differences use the module increments `DV_STEP` and !! `DT_STEP`. class ( ArModel ), intent ( in ) :: model !! Equation of state used to evaluate the critical residual Jacobian. integer , intent ( in ) :: i_comp !! One-based index of the pure component. integer , intent ( in ) :: nc !! Number of components. real ( pr ), intent ( in ) :: V !! Total volume [L]. real ( pr ), intent ( in ) :: T !! Temperature [K]. real ( pr ), intent ( out ) :: J ( 2 , 2 ) !! Jacobian rows (P_V,P_{VV}), columns (V,T). real ( pr ) :: f1_V_plus real ( pr ) :: f1_V_minus real ( pr ) :: f1_T_plus real ( pr ) :: f1_T_minus real ( pr ) :: f2_V_plus real ( pr ) :: f2_V_minus real ( pr ) :: f2_T_plus real ( pr ) :: f2_T_minus real ( pr ) :: P_dummy ! ∂f1/∂V and ∂f2/∂V call residual_critical_eqs ( model , nc , i_comp , V + DV_STEP , T , f1_V_plus , f2_V_plus , P_dummy ) call residual_critical_eqs ( model , nc , i_comp , V - DV_STEP , T , f1_V_minus , f2_V_minus , P_dummy ) J ( 1 , 1 ) = ( f1_V_plus - f1_V_minus ) / ( 2.0_pr * DV_STEP ) J ( 2 , 1 ) = ( f2_V_plus - f2_V_minus ) / ( 2.0_pr * DV_STEP ) ! ∂f1/∂T and ∂f2/∂T call residual_critical_eqs ( model , nc , i_comp , V , T + DT_STEP , f1_T_plus , f2_T_plus , P_dummy ) call residual_critical_eqs ( model , nc , i_comp , V , T - DT_STEP , f1_T_minus , f2_T_minus , P_dummy ) J ( 1 , 2 ) = ( f1_T_plus - f1_T_minus ) / ( 2.0_pr * DT_STEP ) J ( 2 , 2 ) = ( f2_T_plus - f2_T_minus ) / ( 2.0_pr * DT_STEP ) end subroutine jacobian_critical_eqs end module yaeos__critical_pure_point_solver","tags":"","url":"sourcefile/pure_critical_solver.f90.html"},{"title":"dortmund.f90 – yaeos","text":"This file depends on sourcefile~~dortmund.f90~~EfferentGraph sourcefile~dortmund.f90 dortmund.f90 sourcefile~constants.f90 constants.f90 sourcefile~dortmund.f90->sourcefile~constants.f90 sourcefile~dortmund_parameters.f90 dortmund_parameters.f90 sourcefile~dortmund.f90->sourcefile~dortmund_parameters.f90 sourcefile~groups.f90 groups.f90 sourcefile~dortmund.f90->sourcefile~groups.f90 sourcefile~model_parameters.f90 model_parameters.f90 sourcefile~dortmund.f90->sourcefile~model_parameters.f90 sourcefile~temperature_dependence.f90 temperature_dependence.f90 sourcefile~dortmund.f90->sourcefile~temperature_dependence.f90 sourcefile~unifac.f90 unifac.f90 sourcefile~dortmund.f90->sourcefile~unifac.f90 sourcefile~unifac_parameters.f90 unifac_parameters.f90 sourcefile~dortmund.f90->sourcefile~unifac_parameters.f90 sourcefile~dortmund_parameters.f90->sourcefile~constants.f90 sourcefile~dortmund_parameters.f90->sourcefile~model_parameters.f90 sourcefile~groups.f90->sourcefile~constants.f90 sourcefile~model_parameters.f90->sourcefile~constants.f90 sourcefile~temperature_dependence.f90->sourcefile~constants.f90 sourcefile~temperature_dependence.f90->sourcefile~groups.f90 sourcefile~unifac.f90->sourcefile~constants.f90 sourcefile~unifac.f90->sourcefile~groups.f90 sourcefile~unifac.f90->sourcefile~model_parameters.f90 sourcefile~unifac.f90->sourcefile~temperature_dependence.f90 sourcefile~unifac.f90->sourcefile~unifac_parameters.f90 sourcefile~ge_models.f90 ge_models.f90 sourcefile~unifac.f90->sourcefile~ge_models.f90 sourcefile~unifac_parameters.f90->sourcefile~constants.f90 sourcefile~unifac_parameters.f90->sourcefile~model_parameters.f90 sourcefile~ge_models.f90->sourcefile~constants.f90 